# Quality inspect and run

Owner playbook: [`docs/quality-checkpoints.md`](../../docs/quality-checkpoints.md). This pipeline exists only in `vantage-main-server`.

`.cursor/hooks.json` records metadata (start / prompt / tool / stop / end). Hooks do **not** review code. After sessions go idle (20 min) or end (60s), a detached worker may start a checkpoint.

## Inspect

From `vantage-main-server`:

```bash
pnpm quality:status
```

Use `state` from that JSON (`git rev-parse --git-path vantage-quality`). Then read:

- `latest.json` — current or last run
- `runs/<id>/report.json` — stage, changed paths, checks
- `runs/<id>/{review,cleanup,docs,verify}.md` — model reports
- `runs/<id>/{typecheck,lint,test,quality-tests}.log`
- `runs/<id>/changes.patch` — proposed apply
- `worker.log` — background worker
- `events/` — metadata only; no prompt or tool payloads

Statuses: `complete`, `unchanged`, `initialized`, `patch-ready`, `stale`, `failed`, `busy`.

```text
❌ Re-run hook-entry.mjs expecting a review
✅ pnpm quality:status, then open latest.json / runs/<id>/
```

## Run

```bash
pnpm finish-work --provider cursor
pnpm finish-work --provider cursor --no-apply
pnpm quality:pause
pnpm quality:resume
```

Run `finish-work` at a finished-task boundary, not after every turn. Skip it when `VANTAGE_QUALITY_CHILD=1`. `pnpm quality:test` is offline. `node scripts/quality/smoke.mjs cursor` is a paid real-model fixture — do not point it at application code.
